Subject: file-icon: no icon-pair rules and no hover-colour comment for the file tree

What: the sheet drops the `[data-component="filetree"] .filetree-iconpair` rules
(the 16px pair box and its absolutely stacked icons) and the comment saying the
tree shows file-type colours on hover. The monochrome rule stays.
Why: no file tree renders an icon pair any more; each file row mounts the one
monochrome icon it paints. The hover colour never showed: its `group-hover/filetree`
classes need an ancestor with `group/filetree`, which no tree declares, so the
comment described behaviour the code never had.

diff --git a/src/components/file-icon.css b/src/components/file-icon.css
index 1004df41f1..a27d89ee0c 100644
--- a/src/components/file-icon.css
+++ b/src/components/file-icon.css
@@ -5,22 +5,6 @@
   height: 16px;
 }
 
-/*
-  File tree: show monochrome weak icons by default.
-  On hover, show the original file-type colors.
-*/
 [data-component="filetree"] .filetree-icon--mono {
   color: var(--icon-base);
 }
-
-[data-component="filetree"] .filetree-iconpair {
-  position: relative;
-  display: inline-flex;
-  width: 16px;
-  height: 16px;
-}
-
-[data-component="filetree"] .filetree-iconpair .ui-file-icon {
-  position: absolute;
-  inset: 0;
-}
